  "notes": "St. Louis chant-rap over Memphis/Tay-Keith-lineage beats, and the most extreme entry in this batch in two directions at once: the hardest, most syncopated kick (`densityPerBar` [4,7], `syncopation` 0.7, `tresilloBias` 0.3) and the least melodic content of anything here (`densityPerBar` [1,4], `motifPitchCount` [2,4], `register` starting at 56). The research is blunt — the hook is a spoken/shouted chant, so melodic content is near zero — and a model that ignored that would be a trap beat with her name on it. The `bII` in the families is the Memphis flat-two the lineage carries, and it is the reason `relatedGenres` reaches `phonk`. ⛔ `chords.impliedByRiff` is set: \"often a single low bell/organ motif or no pitched instrument at all beyond the 808 — chant-first construction\". Chord variety comes from `chordDurationBeats` [4,16], three `harmonicRhythm` values and a 34-semitone voicing register. ⚠ `confidence` medium — the research is medium-high on era and collaborator lineage and only medium on internals. The INFERRED parameters are the exact kick figures and `bass808.distortion: heavy`; \"crunchy, saturated drum bus\" and \"deliberately gritty\" are the words behind them, not a measurement. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts. ⚠ **The countermelody reached only 950 distinct answers in 1000 seeds against a floor of 980**, so it was given range: densityRatio 0.45. A counter is combinatorial in the styles it may pick, its density against the melody, and the phrase length it answers inside — one style over a thin density inside a single phrase length has almost nothing a seed can vary.",
